window.products.push({"id":160449,"name":"WR60X26866 Refrigerator Evaporator Fan Motor Fit (OEM) for Almost All GE Refrigerators Replace# WR60X26033, WR60X10341, WR60X10356, WR60X10357, WR60X2","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":33.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61rDtVaKYmL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"PRODUCT INFORMATION - WR60X26866 Refrigerator Evaporator Fan Motor, Replacement Models WR60X29099, WR02X13733, WR60X10341, WR60X10356, WR60X1 037, WR60X24303, WR60X26030, WR60X4033, V80E14MS2A3- 57A61. The upgraded fans look different from the original parts and have the same dimensions and function. PRODUCT FUNCTION - WR60X26866 refrigerator fan motor circulates air through the fresh food compartment for efficient cooling.Perfectly fixes a series of problems such as abnormal refrigerator temperature and abnormal noise from the fan motor. Easy to install. You can fix it yourself, enjoy the joy of DIY repair. (Take photos of your unit prior to disassembly, it will save time during the reassembly). COMPATIBLE MODELS - WR60X26866 evaporator fan compatible with GE refrigerator models: CFE28TP2MBS1, CFE28USHNSS, CWE23SP2MBS1, CYE22TP2MBS1, DFE28JELCDS, GFD28GBLBTS, GFE26GGHEBB, PFE28KELFDS, PWE23KSKDSS, PYE22KSKBSS, GYE22HMKEES. etc - Details page lists compatible models. You can contact us. We will help you to confirm whether WR60X26866 is suitable for your refrigerator. MAKES REFRIGERATOR RUN LIKE NEW - Fixes following symptoms: 1. Refrigerator isn't cooling; 2. Freezer section is cold but fridge is not; 3. Evaporator coils are covered in frost; (Frosty Evaporator Coils) 4. Icemaker not making ice; 5. Unusual loud noise from the freezer. EASY TO INSTALL - It only takes a few simple steps to complete the installation and tools needed for this repair project is just a screwdriver. First disconnect the power, then slide the crisper drawer out, remove the panel, pull the old fan out, and replace the new one. Repair refrigerator by yourself, you can save up to 90% of your budget compared to buying new one. Remember to unplug refrigerator from power source as a safety precaution.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61rDtVaKYmL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PFCKE","source_asin":"B0BD4W3GGS","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-160449","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BD4W3GGS","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B0BD4W3GGS","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
